  "method": "every hair cell of 25 px or more (outfit.cells) labelled by eye from zoomed crops (tools/hairtag/truthpic.py); cells holding several families cut along the drawn lines (snapped) and straight across their gaps; the shadow tone in a zone below the head splits the under layer"
 },
 "rules": [
  "one drawn lock, one family: family boundaries run along the drawn lines where they exist and straight across their gaps (cuts snapped to the lines between waypoints)",
  "the under layer is drawn in the shadow tone: in a zone below the head (front rows 305+, profile 265+, back 270+) hair darker than 0.75 is lower_back unless a seed says otherwise; in the back the lit lock tips below the dark band (rows 352+) are lower_back too",
  "the ahoge ends at the head's outline (a straight cut across its base)",
  "the flick tips at the outer silhouette (cut straight across the base where the flick leaves the mass's outline) accept flyaways or their mass's families: hair_breakdown draws them as flyaway strands, the body sheet joins them to the mass",
  "the strands under the buns (a cell each) accept flyaways or their bun (bun tails)",
  "clips drawn in the hair colour (the crab) are none",
  "the side of the head above the side lock (front: the temple strip down to the eyes' top; profile: from the fringe's back line to the star) accepts bangs or side_locks; below the eyes' top the face-framing lock is side_locks",
  "the outer masses behind the side locks, lit, accept side_locks or upper_back (hair_breakdown paints them side-lock yellow with upper-back purple at the edge); the inner locks by the jaw accept side_locks or lower_back",
  "the profile's far-bun peek accepts either bun (as the outfit truth)",
  "the three-quarter's mass is unresolved (any mass family): only buns by side, the ahoge, the clips and the side lock under the star are scored there"
 ],
 "calls": [
  "the flick tips as flyaways-or-mass (front 4, back 4, profile 1 at the back): hair_breakdown's green strands sit at the body sheet's flicks, which the body sheet draws joined to the mass",
  "the shadow tone below the head as the under layer (lower_back), which puts the back's central lit lobe (down to the V at row 355) in the upper back",
  "the temple strip and the profile's side-of-head region as bangs-or-side_locks, the outer masses as side_locks-or-upper_back",
  "the crab as none (the masks label it hair)",
  "the profile's small flick at the side lock's back edge (the 'crescent over the side lock') is labelled with its lock (side_locks|upper_back), not as a flyaway"
 ]
